<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PermissionSet xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        This comment is INSIDE the root element deliberately - a comment above the root
        breaks `sf` at source conversion with "unable to find matching parent xml file".
        Broker_Protection_Access / DPEG_Admin_Access are the precedents for this pattern;
        it is used here because the rationale is longer than the 255-character cap on
        <description>.

        WHY THIS IS ITS OWN SET (added 2026-08-09, Tranche 3A, decision D15/Q1; the name is
        the one the design fixed in option (d)). It is the disposition twin of
        Acquisition_Deal_Driver and follows that precedent rather than folding the grant
        into DPEG_Disposition_Edit. The gate is TWO-FACTOR: assignment of this set, which
        carries the FLS, is factor (a); User.Disposition_Driver__c = true is factor (b).
        Putting the FLS on the broad disposition edit set would hand factor (a) to that
        set's whole population as a side effect of editing dispositions, leaving a
        one-factor gate - the exact widening RecordStageAdvanceService's and
        OpportunityActionPermissionService's headers say a membership check must not
        introduce. A broad set is also redeployed far more often, which matters because a
        PermissionSet deploy REPLACES its entire grant list rather than merging into it
        (measured twice on this project, 2026-08-05 and 2026-08-06).

        WHY THE FLS GRANT IS LOAD-BEARING AND NOT COSMETIC. The gate reads
        User.Disposition_Driver__c WITH USER_MODE. USER_MODE THROWS on a field the running
        principal cannot read - it does not degrade - and the service converts that throw to
        false. Separately, a field deployed through the Metadata API arrives carrying no
        field permissions of its own, which is why this grant ships in the same change as
        the field rather than being left to be added later. Without it the two-factor gate
        has no reachable true branch for anyone, and the failure presents as a quiet denial
        rather than as an error.

        ASSIGNMENT IS AN ORG ACTION, NOT DEPLOYABLE METADATA. Deploying this set grants
        nobody anything until it is assigned, and factor (b) must also be set on each
        driver's own User record. A smoke test performed as an administrator exercises
        neither factor - acceptance-test as a real disposition-driver persona.
    -->
    <description>Marks the disposition deal driver: grants read on User.Disposition_Driver__c so the disposition stage quick actions show only for holders whose Disposition_Driver__c = true. Not assigned to approvers.</description>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>false</editable>
        <field>User.Disposition_Driver__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <hasActivationRequired>false</hasActivationRequired>
    <label>Disposition Deal Driver</label>
</PermissionSet>
